    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9d570853f81d44cebc1e329c1e44ecba",
      "statement": "Cloudflare's telemetry/keys and telemetry/values endpoints ignore the filters they accept (verified against a live account), so constrained discovery (Worker bindings or caller-supplied filters) is derived from a filtered telemetry/query sample instead; separately, a log's own fields are returned nested under source but indexed under their bare name, so observabilityFieldKey accepts the source.-prefixed alias everywhere a caller names a field — a rewrite that cannot widen a query because the binding's own $metadata.service condition is a separate AND term that is never rewritten.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/gatekeeper-cloudflare/README.md#L62-L85",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:98133a474679e7d5c4ec03b325a1500ff5dd0beb3263470e32b279777b1685a3:"
        },
