    {
      "id": "claim_14d3acc963a0429d81994b47e827362c",
      "statement": "Provider error messages can quote a caller-supplied filter value back, so CloudflareObservabilityApiError carries Cloudflare's numeric codes for the audit log while the message travels only to the caller who caused it; because Cloudflare can return a message with no numeric code, the error separately records whether the message is the provider's or ours, and an uncoded provider failure is logged as a bare status (fail-closed).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/gatekeeper-cloudflare/README.md#L90-L101",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:45d2b545dc2c93230f8722e4230b5a4e956e0d1f6b460d3c04d35db1c947ed6e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d43bee18a4ef4176aead108a36f377bc",
      "statement": "Cloudflare's /accounts endpoint pages at 20 per page by default, so the account walk paginates to the end (bounded at 500 accounts) with a mid-walk failure yielding the partial list — a single unpaginated GET would silently hide accounts past the first page.",
